---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
import { courseUrl } from "../data/course";
---

<Base
  title="About, Jamal Mammadzada"
  description="About Jamal Mammadzada: a student researcher and engineer in Allen, Texas working on machine learning, robotics, security, and technical education."
>
  <section class="wrap page-head">
    <p class="mono">About</p>
    <h1 class="h-lg">About</h1>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="bio">
    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="about-body">
        <h2 class="sr-only" id="bio">Biography</h2>

        <p class="lede">
          I'm a junior at {site.school}, in the IB Diploma Programme, graduating
          in {site.graduation.split(" ")[1]}. Most of my time outside class goes
          into building things and teaching people how to build things.
        </p>

        <p>
          What I keep coming back to is the seam between software and something
          physical or consequential. A model that classifies images is a
          contained problem. A model that has to identify robots in shaky phone
          footage from row 20, so a strategy team can decide who to pick, is a
          different one. When it's wrong, a team picks the wrong partner, and
          most of the interesting work ends up happening around the model, not
          inside it.
        </p>

        <p>
          That's roughly the shape of everything on this site. On the scouting
          platform, the hard part turned out to be knowing which outputs you can
          trust. Most of the engineering in the hardening framework went into not
          breaking the machine. The cryptography course ends on a release
          decision instead of a definitions quiz. And at Eaglets I don't design
          the kits, I run the camps, which means the constraint I'm working
          against is a nine-year-old with forty minutes and an adult who has
          never seen a breadboard.
        </p>

        <p>
          The research side is the other half, and it runs on the same instinct.
          I began my extended essay in 2025. It asks how far Itô calculus gets
          you when solving stochastic differential equations, and where each
          kind of exact answer runs out. My physics investigation
          measured whether a warm capacitor discharges differently than a cold
          one, and the data came back disagreeing with my hypothesis, which was
          the most useful thing about it.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h-md about-sub">Teaching</h2>

        <p>
          A lot of what I do is teaching, and I didn't plan that. I've taught
          Java and object-oriented programming, Python and C++ and robotics at
          camps, programming fundamentals to kids, and now a cryptography course
          for adults.
        </p>

        <p>
          It has made me a better engineer. You can't teach something you only
          understand well enough to use. Trying
          to explain why a certain design is right to someone who has no reason
          to take your word for it exposes the parts you were taking on faith
          fast.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h-md about-sub">What I'm looking for</h2>

        <p>
          Research programs, internships, and collaborations where I'd be working
          on real systems with people who know more than I do. I'm most
          interested in machine learning applied to physical systems, computer
          vision, security, and mathematical modeling, but I care more about the
          problem being real than about which of those boxes it falls into.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="about-side">
        <div class="portrait">
          <img
            src="/img/jamal-frc-pit.jpg"
            alt="Jamal Mammadzada in the FRC Team 5417 pit, wearing safety goggles and an Eagle Robotics shirt."
            width="934"
            height="1082"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </div>

        <div class="side-block">
          <p class="mono side-head">Currently</p>
          <ul role="list">
            <li>{site.school}, class of {site.graduation.split(" ")[1]}</li>
            <li>{site.program}</li>
            {site.coursework.map((c) => <li>{c}</li>)}
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="side-block">
          <p class="mono side-head">Working on</p>
          <ul role="list">
            <li><a href="/work/frcmob/">FRCMOB</a>: on-device match breakdown, team workspaces, native apps, and 2027 season readiness</li>
            <li><a href="/work/eaglets/">Eaglets</a>: 2026–27 officer training and camp curriculum</li>
            <li><a href="/work/hardening/">Windows hardening</a>: security automation and rollback safety</li>
            <li><a href="/work/cryptography/">Cryptography course</a>: lectures, activities, and assessment materials</li>
            <li><a href="/research/">Independent research</a>: stochastic calculus and SDE solvability</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="side-block">
          <p class="mono side-head">Based in</p>
          <ul role="list">
            <li>{site.location}</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="side-block">
          <p class="mono side-head">Elsewhere</p>
          <ul role="list">
            <li><a href={site.githubUrl} rel="me noopener">github.com/{site.github}</a></li>
            {courseUrl && (
              <li><a href={courseUrl} rel="noopener">Udemy course</a></li>
            )}
            <li><a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>Email</a></li>
            <li><a href={site.resume}>Résumé (PDF)</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-head {
    padding-top: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem);
  }

  .page-head .mono {
    margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
  }

  .about-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 15rem);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    align-items: start;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding-top: 2.25rem;
  }

  .about-body {
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .about-body .lede {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .about-sub {
    margin: 2.75rem 0 1rem;
  }

  .about-side {
    position: sticky;
    top: 6rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.75rem;
  }

  .portrait {
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
    line-height: 0;
    background: var(--paper-2);
  }

  .portrait img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    filter: saturate(0.94);
  }

  .side-block {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding-top: 0.85rem;
  }

  .side-head {
    margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .side-block ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    font-size: var(--fs-ui);
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .sr-only {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    padding: 0;
    margin: -1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    white-space: nowrap;
    border: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .about-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .about-side {
      position: static;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(180px, 1fr));
    }
  }
</style>
